Z||000000||pHoOl||12-02-2000||05:31 PM||||Are there any of these Autocrosses in michigan?  if so where?  I haven't heard about any, but i'd love to try it sometime.  Also, does it completely rape your car by doing them?  like trans and engine and suspension?  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Greg Piet||12-03-2000||02:26 AM||||GOTO <A HREF="http://www.scca.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.scca.org</A> <BR>you can get to the regional info websites from there.<P>Well it IS racing so yes it is hard on the car.  Do you on a regular basis push the car to its ABSOLUTE performance limits(except top speed)?  I thought not...  So yes there will be added wear on the car (especially brakes and tires).  If you drive like a tool on the track youll grind gears thus killing your tranny, and if you put faith in the stock rev limiter and press in the clutch and at the same time press down on the gas, there is a good chance you'll kill your motor by over revving it.  And if you happen to completely spaz out you will be like a guy in my region who took daddys 1999 Firebird out without permission, and pressed on the gas when he should have pressed on the brake in a spin, thus sliding really off course into a chain link fence.<P>But by weighing all the extra wear on the car versus the fun factor I think it is well worth it.||||reg||1
